// t_36492ad8 commit 2.  Measured against sce-cgc 475.
// A DEFAULTED inout PARAMETER STILL RANKS.  Beside a plain one-parameter
// overload, the one-argument call TIES and the reference refuses:
//     error C1101: ambiguous overloaded function reference "f"
// in BOTH declaration orders, exactly as a plain `float k=.5` second
// parameter does.  This is the row that refutes an arity-exclusion model:
// excluding the defaulted inout candidate would leave f(float4) the unique
// winner and ACCEPT a program the reference refuses.  (Fable's ruling,
// codex's six cells; a build that did exclude it accepted all four.)
void f(float4 c, inout float4 o = float4(0,0,0,1)) { o = o + c; }
void f(float4 c) { }
float4 main(float4 t : TEXCOORD0) : COLOR { f(t); return t; }
